        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Alopecurus, Echeveria\n- Places: Eurasia, northern Africa, the Americas, Australia, various islands, Central America, Mexico, northwestern South America\n- Concepts: geographic distribution, native range, naturalization, plant taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- Alopecurus is common across temperate and subtropical parts of Eurasia, northern Africa, and the Americas.\n- Alopecurus is also naturalized in Australia and on various islands.\n- Echeveria is a large genus of flowering plants in the Crassulaceae family.\n- Echeveria is native to semi-desert areas of Central America, Mexico, and northwestern South America.",
